.Dd August 3, 2026
.Dt ROOK-CTL 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rook-ctl
.Nd rook's control socket protocol
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Every running
.Xr rook 1
serves a Unix-domain control socket that exposes the whole application:
what every pane shows, what the renderer drew, and every input the
keyboard could produce.
It exists so that scripts \(em and above all agents \(em can verify their own
work against the real app instead of asking a human to look.
.Pp
The rook binary is its own client \(em any subcommand it does not
recognize locally is sent as a verb, reply on stdout,
.Ql err
as exit 1:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rook panes
.Ed
.Pp
And the protocol is plain enough that anything else can speak it raw:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'panes\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
.Ed
.Ss Connection
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
Socket path:
.Ev ROOK_SOCK ,
default
.Pa /tmp/rook.sock .
A sandboxed instance
.Pq Ql rook --config=DIR
serves
.Pa DIR/rook.sock .
.It
Commands are newline-delimited, several per connection if you like.
A line over 4096 bytes drops the connection.
.It
Replies are plain text.
Errors start with
.Ql err .
.It
When the socket binds, the app prints
.Ql rook ctl: listening on <path>
to stderr \(em the readiness signal.
.It
A second instance finding its socket already served by a live rook runs
.Em without
a control surface and says so on stderr; set
.Ev ROOK_SOCK
before launching to give it one.
A stale socket file left by a dead instance is unlinked and reused.
.It
There is no authentication.
Filesystem permissions on the socket are the whole security model:
whoever can connect can read every pane, drive input, take screenshots,
and
.Cm quit
the app.
.El
.Ss Pane addressing
A verb may carry a pane id suffix:
.Ql dump@3 ,
.Ql type@3 <text> .
Honoured by
.Cm dump , Cm type , Cm enter , Cm ctrlc , Cm key ;
everything else acts on the focused pane or the app.
Ids come from
.Cm panes .
.Sh READING THE APP
.Bl -tag -width "workspaces"
.It Cm dump Ns Op @ Ns Ar id
The pane's content as text:
.Ql pane <id> grid <c>x<r>
then the screen \(em the terminal's plain text, or the editor's buffer view.
The ground truth for
.Dq what is rook showing .
.It Cm panes
One line per pane across all spaces and tabs:
space, tab, id, pixel rect, grid, zoom flag, and whether it is a terminal
or an editor
.Pq with the document name .
.Ql *
marks the focused pane and current space.
.It Cm tabs
Tabs of the current space with pane counts and bell flags.
.It Cm workspaces
The workspaces, freshly read: declared ones from the environment graph
.Pq see Xr rook-config 5 ,
each followed by its git worktrees, derived live from the repo's own
.Pa .git/worktrees
records.
.Ql name<TAB>root
per line
.Pq children as Ql parent/name ,
or
.Ql none .
.It Cm docs
Open documents and how many panes hold each \(em one file open twice is one
document.
.It Cm lsp
Language-server state: enabled or not, per-server status, and the focused
editor's diagnostics
.Pq gutter counts and each message .
Then its completion ring:
.Ql cpl off ,
or
.Ql cpl on
with the prefix, the selected row, and
.Ql semantic:yes
once a server's answer has been folded in \(em which is what
distinguishes a menu of the buffer's own words from one that knows what
the cursor is inside of.
Then every declared language that has no server running, and why:
.Ql language zig declared zls
(declared, nothing started yet),
.Ql language python resolving <root>
(a resolver plugin was asked and has not answered),
or
.Ql language python refused <root> \(em <the resolver's words> .
With no catalog compiled in, "which languages does this rook know about"
is a question about the CONFIG, and this is where it is answered.
.Pp
Then the hover float:
.Ql hover off ,
or
.Ql hover on
with the laid-out row count, the first visible row and the language its
fence claimed.
The float's text is in
.Cm dump
already; this is the part the grid cannot say, which is how much of the
document is below the fold.
.It Cm statusbar
The chrome, with hit-test coordinates: workspace/branch/cwd segments,
top-bar and status-bar layouts, tab style, activity-bar rail entries.
.It Cm whichkey
The which-key sheet:
.Ql closed ,
or armed state plus each visible chord hint with its screen position.
.It Cm palette
The command palette:
.Ql closed ,
or its mode
.Pq commands, files, workspaces, plugins, actions ,
current filter, and rows; a
.Ql *
marks the selection.
Files mode adds the index root and count.
Actions mode is the code-action picker: title and kind per row, plus
.Ql deferred
for one whose edit the server has not computed yet
.Pq picking it costs a resolve round trip
and
.Ql command
for one rook cannot run.
.It Cm sidepane
The side panel:
.Ql closed ,
or which edge and tenant
.Pq plugin, config, search
plus
.Ql focus:panel
or
.Ql focus:panes
\(em who holds the keys \(em and the tenant's rows.
A focused panel eats plain typing; ^H
.Pq away from a right-edge panel
hands the keys back, ^L from the edge pane walks in.
.Pp
The search tenant has two producers, so it reports
.Ql kind:grep
or
.Ql kind:references
alongside
.Ql label: ,
which is the query for the first and the symbol for the second.
The box and the list can disagree \(em
.Ql gr
leaves whatever you last typed in the box \(em so read
.Ql kind:
rather than
.Ql query: .
.It Cm welcome
The onboarding screen, if open, and its choices.
A FRESH instance
.Pq say, a Ql --config=DIR No sandbox
opens this chooser over the first pane, where it eats keystrokes \(em an
Enter meant for the shell picks a config language instead.
Check it before driving a new instance;
.Ql press ESC
dismisses.
.It Cm attention
The attention inbox: one
.Ql seq<TAB>from<TAB>title<TAB>body
line per raise
.Pq see Xr rook-plugin 7 ,
or
.Ql none .
.It Cm search
Copy-mode search state of the focused terminal.
.It Cm clipboard , Cm ime , Cm notify
Pasteboard content and write-allowance; input-method state; last user
notification.
Introspection for tests.
.It Cm activity
Per-pane pty liveness:
.Ql id<TAB>out_ms<TAB>in_ms<TAB>fg<TAB>cwd
\(em milliseconds since the child last wrote and since the human last
typed there
.Pq physical keyboard only; \-1 = never ,
the foreground program, the shell's working directory.
Output and input travel different directions through different code
paths, so
.Dq the TUI is redrawing
and
.Dq the human is present
are two separate facts.
Plugins get the same answer as JSON through the
.Ql panes.activity
grant \(em see
.Xr rook-plugin 7 .
.It Cm monitor Op Cm live | disk
Open the resource monitor in the focused pane, optionally selecting a
section.
Opening is idempotent \(em unlike the
.Ql <leader>r
chord, which toggles \(em so a scripted
.Ql monitor disk
on an already-open monitor selects the tab instead of closing it.
The pane's contents are readable through
.Cm dump
like any other, and come from the same fill the window draws.
.It Cm disk
The reclaim table, one line per classified directory:
.Ql bytes<TAB>class<TAB>category<TAB>path .
Preceded by a
.Ql volume
line and, once a scan has finished, a
.Ql reclaimable
line totalling each class.
.Pp
The class is the column that matters, not the size.
.Cm regenerable
is tool output that rebuilds,
.Cm refetchable
is a cache that re-downloads, and
.Cm keep
is data \(em agent transcripts, downloads, VM images \(em which the
monitor will report and never offer to delete.
Directories the classifier has no opinion about \(em
.Ql build ,
.Ql dist ,
.Ql out
\(em are deliberately absent: they are hand-authored often enough that a
delete button on them would be a data-loss bug waiting for the right
repository.
.Pp
Sizes are on-disk blocks with hardlinks counted once, matching
.Xr du 1 Ns 's
.Fl s Fl x
exactly.
A scan is started from the monitor with
.Ql s
and walks the focused pane's shell working directory.
.It Cm hud
The performance HUD line.
.It Cm stats
The perf counters report.
.Ql stats reset
zeroes them.
.It Cm boottime
Startup phase timings in microseconds.
.It Cm version
.Ql rook <version> build=<id> .
.El
.Sh DRIVING INPUT
.Bl -tag -width "nskey k m c"
.It Cm run Ar name
Execute a registry command by id
.Pq Ql pane.split-right , Ql config.apply , ... ,
alias, or
.Ql tab.select-N .
.Cm commands
lists every id; this is the highest-level way to drive rook.
.It Cm commands
The command registry:
.Ql id<TAB>category: title<TAB>keys<TAB>:ExName
per command.
Every command is also an ex-command inside the editor.
.It Cm press Ar key
One keystroke through the full chrome pipeline
.Pq leader, which-key, palette :
a single character or
.Cm TAB , SPACE , ESC , RET , BS .
Replies
.Ql consumed
.Pq chrome ate it
or
.Ql typed
.Pq it reached the pane .
.It Cm type Ns Oo @ Ns Ar id Oc Ar text
Write
.Ar text
into the pane's pty
.Pq or editor
verbatim.
.It Cm enter Ns Op @ Ns Ar id , Cm ctrlc Ns Op @ Ns Ar id
Send return / interrupt to the pane.
.It Cm key Ns Oo @ Ns Ar id Oc Ar hex
Raw bytes to the pane, hex-encoded
.Pq Ql 1b5b41 No is Up Arrow .
.It Cm nskey Ar keycode mods-hex chars
A synthetic AppKit key event, for chords the higher layers cannot spell.
.It Cm paste Op Ar text
With
.Ar text :
paste it
.Pq Ql \een No escapes supported .
Bare: paste the real pasteboard, echoing what was pasted.
.It Cm click Ar x y , Cm drag Ar x1 y1 x2 y2 , Cm wheel Ar x y lines
Mouse, in pixels.
.It Cm copy
The current selection's text, or
.Ql err nothing selected .
.El
.Sh LAYOUT AND WINDOW
.Bl -tag -width "winsize w h"
.It Cm split Cm right Ns | Ns Cm down
Split the focused pane.
.It Cm focus Ar id Ns | Ns Cm left Ns | Ns Cm right Ns | Ns Cm up Ns | Ns Cm down
Move focus by id or direction.
.It Cm zoom
Toggle pane zoom.
.It Cm close
Close the focused pane
.Pq the cmd-W path .
.It Cm tab Cm new Ns | Ns Cm next Ns | Ns Cm prev Ns | Ns Ar n
Tab management.
.It Cm winsize Ar w h
Resize the window
.Pq points, minimum 100 .
.It Cm fullscreen
Toggle fullscreen.
.It Cm palette-open
Open the command palette.
.It Cm edit Ar path
Open
.Ar path
in the editor.
Prefer absolute paths: a relative one resolves against the
.Em app's
working directory, not yours.
.Pq this is the verb Xr re 1 speaks .
.It Cm shot Ar path
Write a PNG of the window to
.Ar path
\(em rook's own Metal drawable, so no screen-recording permission is
involved.
Fails
.Ql err busy
or
.Ql err timeout
.Pq 2s .
.El
.Sh CONFIG AND PLUGINS
.Bl -tag -width "plugin-show name"
.It Cm env
Pending configuration changes:
.Ql checking ,
.Ql no pending changes ,
.Ql broken
followed by the config program's own output, or
.Ql pending:N
with one
.Ql + ,
.Ql - ,
.Ql ~
row per changed node.
See
.Xr rook-config 5 .
.It Cm env Cm apply
Apply the pending diff \(em the whole diff; there is no partial apply.
.It Cm plugins
Every declared plugin:
name, load mode, state, grants, capabilities it asked for, version,
and \(em for an up, sourced, unpinned plugin \(em its
.Ql sha256=
ready for pinning.
Failures carry their reason.
.It Cm plugin-show Ar name
Open the plugin panel on
.Ar name .
.It Cm worktree Cm add Ar workspace name
Carve a git worktree of the declared
.Ar workspace
on branch
.Ar name
.Pq created if new ,
under
.Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/rook/worktrees/ .
Replies
.Ql ok <path>
\(em the path is the point; cd there.
The new checkout appears in
.Cm workspaces
immediately, derived from git.
.It Cm worktree Cm remove Ar workspace name
Remove that worktree and delete its branch.
Refuses, in order: commits on the branch the workspace's HEAD cannot
reach
.Pq merge them first ,
and a dirty checkout
.Pq git's own refusal, quoted verbatim .
A branch git will not delete is kept and said so.
.It Cm plugin Ar name op Op Ar params-json
Call a plugin op directly and print its raw answer.
Refused with
.Ql err not granted
unless the config grants
.Ar op .
See
.Xr rook-plugin 7 .
.El
.Sh LIFECYCLE
.Bl -tag -width "stats reset"
.It Cm quit
.Ql ok ,
then immediate exit \(em no teardown, the socket file is left behind
.Pq the next launch cleans it up .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Is the app up, and what is it showing?
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'version\enpanes\endump\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Drive the leader chord and see what the which-key sheet offers:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'press SPACE\enwhichkey\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Prove a change visually:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'shot /tmp/rook.png\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
.Ed
.Pp
Run a command the way the palette would:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf 'run pane.split-right\en' | nc -U /tmp/rook.sock
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr rook 1 ,
.Xr rook-config 5 ,
.Xr rook-plugin 7
.Sh CAVEATS
.Cm shot , winsize , fullscreen , hud , stats , quit
match the whole line and so cannot take a pane suffix.
.Pp
.Cm plugin
is matched as a prefix, so a misspelling like
.Ql pluginx
is parsed as a plugin call rather than an unknown verb.
